(3935354, 556527, 69040, '<td valign="top">I love that song . . . probably my fav. beatles song, def my fav beatles album . . Not a bad shot either. I wanted to comment during challenge but I dont'' vote when I enter.<br/> <br/>edit: Which BW conversion did you use, and did you dodge/burn or curves, or both? Great contrast, if you wouldn''t mind a bit of insight. Again, nice shot, very ''cute.'' (No sarcasm)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-25 09:50:58.</i></td>', 'I love that song . . . probably my fav. beatles song, def my fav beatles album . . Not a bad shot either. I wanted to comment during challenge but I dont'' vote when I enter. edit: Which BW conversion did you use, and did you dodge/burn or curves, or both? Great contrast, if you wouldn''t mind a bit of insight. Again, nice shot, very ''cute.'' (No sarcasm)', '2007-07-25 10:49:32.000000', '2007-07-25 10:50:58.000000', 0),
(3935377, 556732, 69040, '<td valign="top">Well, I learned a lesson on this one. Though the shot isn''t incredible, I figure I could have upped my score by quite a bit if I made my title "Confidentially (Sealing Wax)". I didn''t think this was too ambiguous, but I understand people don''t have forever to evaluate my shot.<br/> <br/>Anyways, I wish people would skip the pic and not vote if they really "don''t get it." Especially since the technicals on this shot are faily solid. The high number of 1,2, and 3 votes hurt.<br/> <br/>It is sort of rewarding to get the impressive comments and I find it ironic that my worst scoring photo is my first to get faved. Anyways, like I said this is a nice lesson -- better to err on the obvious / safe side when titling shots on dpc. Still, a little dissapointing that you have to practically shove it into the voters face . . .</td>', 'Well, I learned a lesson on this one. Though the shot isn''t incredible, I figure I could have upped my score by quite a bit if I made my title "Confidentially (Sealing Wax)". I didn''t think this was too ambiguous, but I understand people don''t have forever to evaluate my shot. Anyways, I wish people would skip the pic and not vote if they really "don''t get it." Especially since the technicals on this shot are faily solid. The high number of 1,2, and 3 votes hurt. It is sort of rewarding to get the impressive comments and I find it ironic that my worst scoring photo is my first to get faved. Anyways, like I said this is a nice lesson -- better to err on the obvious / safe side when titling shots on dpc. Still, a little dissapointing that you have to practically shove it into the voters face . . .', '2007-07-25 10:56:48.000000', NULL, 0),
